# PrintOptimizer Pro

PrintOptimizer Pro is a beginner-friendly desktop application for simplifying 3D printing setup. It helps users choose settings with no slicer knowledge required by asking only a few simple questions: printer, filament, print type, and priority.

## Features

- Beginner-friendly optimizer flow
- Tkinter desktop GUI with dark theme
- Printer and filament databases
- Automatic setting generation
- AI-style prompt recommendation using natural language
- Queue manager for GCODE files
- Profile save/load/import/export
- Analysis panel with quality, strength, speed, and time estimates

## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- Tkinter (usually included with Python for Windows)

## Run

```bash
python main.py
```

## Project Structure

- `main.py` - app entry point
- `core/` - optimization, analysis, queue, and profile logic
- `ui/` - tab-based interface modules
- `data/` - JSON profile and machine info

## Notes

This project is designed for Windows-first desktop use and is intentionally simple for beginners while still offering professional recommendations.
